From d8a446b2b329a069c16e3afb6cb12a27cc643214 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude-sandbox <sandbox@local>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 10:32:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] mdblist: restructure the settings screen around watch
 state, not ratings

The screen was titled "MDBList Ratings" and filed under Integrations as an
external ratings provider. It now holds watch tracking, which is the same
category as Trakt, and the Watch Progress picker that governs it lived
only inside the Trakt screen behind a CONNECTED gate - so a user without
a Trakt account could not reach it at all.

- Retitle away from "Ratings" and group the eight rating toggles under
  their own heading, so the screen reads as an account rather than a
  badge configuration.
- Add an account summary: username, plan, and requests spent today
  against the daily ceiling, which matters on a 1,000/day free tier where
  ratings and sync draw on the same budget. Selecting a row refreshes it.
- Mirror the Watch Progress picker in as a second entry point. Same
  DataStore key, same value, same option list and the same rule for
  offering MDBList. The Trakt screen keeps its gate untouched - that gate
  is correct, and reachability is fixed by the second door, not by
  weakening the first.

GET /user gains a typed body and, load-bearing, a no-cache header: the
endpoint answers with Cache-Control: public, max-age=900, so the shared
client would serve a request count a quarter of an hour stale and would
also validate an API key revoked inside that window. The response also
carries store_account_token, which is a credential and is deliberately
left unmapped.

Upstream: NuvioMedia/NuvioTV. MDBList API by linaspurinis.
